 ## Background
-This method is described in an unofficial GitHub repository "3DGS-101" by Chamud, specifically in the section "5.8 A from-scratch NumPy renderer" [S1, unofficial]. It serves as a pedagogical example to demonstrate front-to-back alpha compositing without relying on graphics libraries or GPU-specific optimizations. The approach highlights the mathematical recurrence of compositing while noting the trade-offs of vectorization over all pixels.
